//==
// # A region's boundary, indexed once per face (complexity sweep, chunk R3, TKT-385)
//
// Layer 05-face-meshing. The value the refinement asks its boundary questions of: which
// point pairs are boundary segments (IsConstrained) and whether a new point is strictly inside
// (IsStrictlyInside). Built once per refinement by BoundaryIndexOf (uv-boundary-index.library.plato).

// Region Region's boundary under tolerance Tolerance, indexed. Boundary point i is
// Region.BoundaryPoints[i]; segment i runs from boundary point i to the next point of its loop,
// SegmentEnd[i] (itself for a point hole), on loop SegmentLoop[i]. Next is NextBoundaryTable:
// SegmentEnd[i] on a loop of at least three points, else -1, so Next[i] >= 0 exactly when
// segment i is a boundary segment and a side of the loop's polygon. Raw holds the points as
// plane points (ToPoint2D), Units in tolerance units (InToleranceUnits). Grid lists each segment
// under the cells its box in tolerance units, grown by BoundaryIndexMargin on every side, meets;
// FirstColumn[i] is the first grid column of segment i's box. Usable is false when a point in
// tolerance units is not finite or a tolerance is not positive: then IsStrictlyInsideIndexed
// asks the region itself.
// Removes: the O(L^2) loop search per IsConstrained call (LoopOfBoundaryPoint over LoopOffset)
// and the scan over every boundary segment per IsStrictlyInside call.
type BoundaryIndex
{
    Region: UvRegion;
    Tolerance: UvTolerance;
    Next: Array<Integer>;
    SegmentEnd: Array<Integer>;
    SegmentLoop: Array<Integer>;
    Raw: Array<Point2D>;
    Units: Array<Point2D>;
    Grid: ChartGrid;
    FirstColumn: Array<Integer>;
    Usable: Boolean;
}
